Insurance pools many exposures, converting uncertain individual losses into priced collective obligations.|1,000 independently exposed policyholders share expected claim costs and insurer expenses.|Pooling eliminates correlated catastrophe risk?|No|Yes|Only for large pools
Life, health, general, and liability products insure different events and claims structures.|Health pays qualifying medical costs; liability covers specified third-party obligations.|One policy automatically covers every loss type?|No|Yes|Only if expensive
Term insurance principally protects against specified death risk; savings-linked products combine protection and accumulation under contract terms.|Compare a pure protection premium with a bundled policy's charges and benefits.|Bundled savings guarantees better returns than separate investing?|No|Yes|Only long term
Premiums buy contracted protection; deductibles leave initial loss with the insured; exclusions limit covered events.|Covered loss ₹10 less deductible ₹2 gives ₹8 payment before other limits.|Claim payment is…?|₹8|₹10|₹12
Underwriting selects and prices risk; adverse selection arises when applicants possess relevant private information.|Higher-risk applicants disproportionately buy underpriced coverage.|This can raise…?|Actual claims relative to pricing|Guaranteed insurer profit|Investment yield automatically
Reinsurance transfers specified insurer risks to another insurer subject to contract and counterparty risk.|An insurer cedes a share of qualifying claims.|Reinsurance removes all retained and counterparty risk?|No|Yes|Only for catastrophe cover
Claims reserves and technical provisions estimate future obligations, including incurred unsettled claims.|A reported claim remains unpaid at year-end but creates an estimated obligation.|No payment means no liability necessarily?|No|Yes|Only for long-tail claims
Mortality measures death risk; morbidity illness; frequency claim count; severity loss size.|Expected claims 10 × average severity ₹5 gives ₹50 expected cost.|Doubling severity with unchanged frequency makes expected cost…?|₹100|₹50|₹25
Insurance liability valuation discounts appropriately modelled obligations and incorporates applicable measurement requirements.|A certain ₹110 payment next year at 10% has PV ₹100 before other adjustments.|A lower discount rate increases this liability PV?|Yes|No|Only for life policies
Loss ratios compare claims with defined premium income; expense ratios add costs; combined ratio sums both on a consistent basis.|Loss ratio 70% + expense ratio 25% gives combined ratio 95%.|Underwriting alone is generally profitable at 95% before other effects?|Yes|No|Only at 105%
Embedded value and new-business value estimate shareholder economics under methodology-specific assumptions.|New policies add value only after expected claims, costs, capital, and risk allowances.|Premium growth alone proves value creation?|No|Yes|Only for life insurers
Insurer investment portfolios fund claims and must consider liquidity, duration, credit, and constraints.|Long liabilities are supported by suitable long assets with claim-payment liquidity.|Highest yield is the only objective?|No|Yes|Only for insurers
Asset-liability matching aligns timing, duration, currency, and sensitivity of assets and obligations.|Long-duration liabilities rise faster than short assets when rates fall.|This can weaken…?|Economic surplus|Only premium volume|Only policy count
Solvency capital absorbs adverse outcomes under the relevant regime; requirements differ by jurisdiction and risk.|A catastrophe depletes capital despite previously profitable underwriting.|Past profits guarantee current solvency?|No|Yes|Only if audited
Pensions accumulate retirement resources; annuities provide contractual income and allocate longevity risk.|A life annuity continues under specified terms even if the purchaser lives unusually long.|Longevity exposure depends on…?|Contract guarantees and payment duration|Only current salary|Only deposit balance
Catastrophe risks are correlated; insurance-linked securities transfer specified event risk to investors.|A catastrophe bond may reduce principal after a qualifying trigger.|Its coupon is risk-free because events are rare?|No|Yes|Only outside storm season
